    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** highlights a clear top-tier offensive core, anchored by **James Wood**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**. **James Wood** stands as our highest-rated play at 73.06, benefiting from a prime leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Arrighetti, while **Corbin Carroll** (76.20) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (71.14) provide elite efficiency against Michael King and Melton, respectively. Specifically, **Mickey Moniak** (63.93) is a sneakily strong play; despite his projected bottom-of-the-order slot, his massive platoon advantage against Roki Sasaki and the pitcher's slow delivery\u2014which significantly boosts his stolen base potential\u2014make him a critical asset for our scarcity-driven strategy. Meanwhile, **Josh Naylor** (72.36) continues to feast on favorable pitching matchups, with his score inflated by a strong 19% boost from facing a subpar arm in Phillips.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Cole Young**, who fell just short of the 55-point threshold at 51.08. While **Cole Young** benefits from the same favorable matchup against Phillips as **Josh Naylor**, his bottom-third order placement and lower base projection kept him out of the starting nine in favor of the higher-upside profiles like **Alex Freeland** and **Jose Caballero**. We are keeping a close watch on **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Mickey Moniak**, as their scores are based on pending lineups; any shift higher in the batting order for these three would significantly improve their efficiency ratings.\n\nFinally, we are exercising caution with **Seiya Suzuki** (51.88) and **Austin Riley** (53.79). **Seiya Suzuki** is facing the elite arm of Kremer, which drags his projected efficiency down significantly despite a favorable park factor, while **Austin Riley** continues to contend with tough SP matchups that suppress his raw output. We are opting to lean into our high-speed, high-platoon-advantage hitters today to prioritize categories that move the needle in a 5x5 Roto context, leaving **Isaac Paredes** and **Henry Bolte** on the pine as we monitor weather and lineup pivots throughout the afternoon.",
